# Theme-aware interactive colours

## The bug to avoid

`bg-accent` is a Tailwind v4 utility that resolves to `var(--color-accent)`.
`text-white` is always `#fff`.

In **light mode** the card background is `#fff` and there is NO `--color-accent` defined
unless it is listed in `@theme inline` — so `bg-accent` is a no-op and you get
white text on a white card = invisible.

In **dark mode** `--accent: #34d399` (light mint) — white text on a light green
background also fails WCAG contrast.

## Required approach

### @theme inline (globals.css) — already done

```css
@theme inline {
  --color-accent:    var(--accent);
  --color-accent-fg: var(--accent-fg);  /* contrast-safe fg on accent bg */
}
```

Both variables are defined for light and dark in `:root` / `.dark`.

### Active tabs / selected buttons

```tsx
// ❌ WRONG — text-white fails on light accent bg
className={active ? "bg-accent text-white" : "..."}

// ✅ CORRECT — text-accent-fg is always contrast-safe on --accent bg
className={active ? "bg-accent text-accent-fg" : "..."}
```

### CTA / submit buttons & badges

```tsx
// ❌ WRONG
className="bg-accent text-white px-4 py-2"

// ✅ CORRECT
className="bg-accent text-accent-fg px-4 py-2"
```

## Quick check

After adding any `bg-accent` element, verify that the text class is
`text-accent-fg` (Tailwind utility) or `text-[var(--accent-fg)]` (arbitrary),
never a hard-coded `text-white` or `text-black`.
